WEBVTT

00:00:10.494 --> 00:00:11.927
Sammy!

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.827
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.927
Go!

00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:19.860
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:21.661
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:24.494 --> 00:00:26.793
This is dad's book.

00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:28.661
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off -

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.361
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:32.394 --> 00:00:35.427
I got to find dad. It's the
only think i can think about.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.594
Bethany: now i lay me down to sleep.

00:00:42.628 --> 00:00:44.793
I pray the lord my soul to keep.

00:00:44.827 --> 00:00:47.527
Thy angels watch me through the night

00:00:47.561 --> 00:00:50.294
And keep me safe till morning light.

00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:53.261
Amen.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.760
Night, monkeypuss.

00:01:03.793 --> 00:01:05.594
Daddy?

00:01:05.628 --> 00:01:07.661
Is mommy coming home?

00:01:11.261 --> 00:01:13.527
No, honey.

00:01:13.561 --> 00:01:16.628
She's spending the night at
the hospital with your sister.

00:01:16.661 --> 00:01:17.960
Hey.

00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:20.127
You sleep tight now.

00:03:14.477 --> 00:03:17.677
Dean: yeah, you probably
missed something.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.844
Dude, i ran lexisnexis,
local police reports,

00:03:19.877 --> 00:03:22.144
Newspapers
- I couldn't find a single red flag.

00:03:22.177 --> 00:03:24.244
Are you sure you got
the coordinates right?

00:03:24.278 --> 00:03:25.378
Yeah, i double-Checked.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.710
It's fitchburg, wisconsin.

00:03:26.744 --> 00:03:28.710
Dad wouldn't have sent us coordinates

00:03:28.744 --> 00:03:30.378
If it wasn't important, sammy.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.710
Well, i'm telling you, i looked,

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.744
And all i could find was a
big, steamy pile of nothing.

00:03:33.777 --> 00:03:35.077
If dad's sending us
hunting for something,

00:03:35.111 --> 00:03:36.144
I don't know what.

00:03:36.177 --> 00:03:37.644
Well, maybe he's gonna meet us there.

00:03:37.677 --> 00:03:40.844
Yeah, 'cause he's been so
easy to find up to this point.

00:03:40.877 --> 00:03:43.044
You're a real smartass, you know that?

00:03:43.077 --> 00:03:44.410
Don't worry.

00:03:44.443 --> 00:03:46.810
I'm sure there's something
in fitchburg worth killing.

00:03:46.844 --> 00:03:49.044
Yeah? What makes you so sure?

00:03:49.077 --> 00:03:52.244
Because i'm the oldest,
which means i'm always right.

00:03:52.278 --> 00:03:54.977
No, it doesn't. It totally does.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.111
Well, the waitress thinks

00:04:13.144 --> 00:04:16.278
That the local freemasons
are up to something sneaky,

00:04:16.311 --> 00:04:17.577
But other than that,

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.344
Nobody's heard about
anything weird going on.

00:04:20.378 --> 00:04:23.777
Dean, you got the time?

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.077
10 after 4:00.

00:04:26.111 --> 00:04:27.677
Why?

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.844
What's wrong with this picture?

00:04:35.944 --> 00:04:39.177
School's out, isn't it?

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:40.810
Yeah.

00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:45.311
So where is everybody?

00:04:45.344 --> 00:04:49.077
This place should be
crawling with kids right now.

00:05:02.844 --> 00:05:05.477
It sure is quiet out here.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.278
Yeah, it's a shame.

00:05:07.311 --> 00:05:08.577
Why is that?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.077
You know, kids getting
sick. It's a terrible thing.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.410
How many?

00:05:14.443 --> 00:05:18.944
Just five or six, but
serious, hospital serious.

00:05:18.977 --> 00:05:21.677
A lot of parents are
getting pretty anxious.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.244
They think it's catching.

00:05:36.977 --> 00:05:39.344
Dude, dude, i am not using this i.D.

00:05:39.378 --> 00:05:40.510
Why not?

00:05:40.543 --> 00:05:42.577
Because it says "bikini
inspector" on it.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.543
Don't worry. She won't look that close.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.344
Hell, she won't even ask to see it.

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:47.710
It's all about confidence, sammy.

00:05:48.844 --> 00:05:50.644
Hi.

00:05:50.677 --> 00:05:53.610
I'm dr. Jerry kaplan,
center for disease control.

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:55.744
Can i see some i.D.?

00:05:58.677 --> 00:06:00.911
Yeah, of course.

00:06:03.244 --> 00:06:06.144
Now, could you direct me
to the pediatrics ward?

00:06:06.177 --> 00:06:09.644
Okay, just go down that hall,
turn left, up the stairs.

00:06:09.677 --> 00:06:11.144
You'll see them.

00:06:11.177 --> 00:06:12.977
Right. Thank you.

00:06:13.011 --> 00:06:15.111
See? Told you it would work.

00:06:15.144 --> 00:06:17.911
Follow me. It's upstairs.

00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:53.510
Sam: dean.

00:07:02.844 --> 00:07:04.877
Thanks for seeing us, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:04.911 --> 00:07:06.777
Oh, i'm glad you guys are here.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:09.177
I was just about to call the cdc myself.

00:07:09.211 --> 00:07:10.944
How did you find out anyway?

00:07:10.977 --> 00:07:13.144
Oh, some g.P. - I
forget his name -

00:07:13.177 --> 00:07:16.177
He called atlanta and must
have beat you to the punch.

00:07:16.211 --> 00:07:18.977
So you say you got six cases so far?

00:07:19.011 --> 00:07:21.378
Yeah, in five weeks.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:23.911
At first i thought it
was bacterial pneumonia,

00:07:23.944 --> 00:07:25.044
Not that newsworthy.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.944
But now...

00:07:26.977 --> 00:07:29.111
Now, what?

00:07:29.144 --> 00:07:31.477
The kids aren't
responding to antibiotics.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.777
Their white-Cell
counts keep going down.

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.510
Their immune systems just
aren't doing their job.

00:07:36.543 --> 00:07:39.344
It's like their bodies are wearing out.

00:07:39.378 --> 00:07:40.944
Betty: excuse me, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:40.977 --> 00:07:42.744
You ever see anything like this before?

00:07:42.777 --> 00:07:43.911
Never this severe.

00:07:43.944 --> 00:07:46.443
The way it spreads
- That's a new one for me.

00:07:46.477 --> 00:07:47.710
What do you mean?

00:07:47.744 --> 00:07:49.244
It works its way through families,

00:07:49.278 --> 00:07:52.477
But only the children,
one sibling after another.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.977
You mind if we interview
a few of the kids?

00:07:56.011 --> 00:07:58.144
They're not conscious.

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:00.311
None of them?

00:08:00.344 --> 00:08:02.144
No.

00:08:02.177 --> 00:08:05.344
Can we talk to the parents?

00:08:06.777 --> 00:08:08.710
If you think it'll help.

00:08:08.744 --> 00:08:12.311
Yeah, yeah. Who was your
most recent admission?

00:08:12.344 --> 00:08:14.577
I should get back to my girls.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.844
We understand that,

00:08:15.877 --> 00:08:18.577
And we really appreciate
you talking to us.

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.644
Now, you say mary's the oldest?

00:08:20.677 --> 00:08:21.877
13.

00:08:21.911 --> 00:08:24.077
Okay, and she came down
with it first, right?

00:08:24.111 --> 00:08:25.177
And then...

00:08:25.211 --> 00:08:27.344
Bethany the next night.

00:08:27.378 --> 00:08:29.244
Within 24 hours?

00:08:29.278 --> 00:08:32.011
I guess.

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:35.111
Look, i already went through
all this with the doctor.

00:08:35.144 --> 00:08:37.144
Right. Just a few more
questions, if you don't mind.

00:08:37.177 --> 00:08:39.077
How do you think they caught pneumonia?

00:08:39.111 --> 00:08:41.278
Were they out in the
cold, anything like that?

00:08:41.311 --> 00:08:43.443
No, we think it was an open window.

00:08:43.477 --> 00:08:45.777
Both times?

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:49.378
The first time, i don't really remember,

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:50.944
But the second time for sure,

00:08:50.977 --> 00:08:53.977
And i know i closed it
before i put bethany to bed.

00:08:54.011 --> 00:08:55.510
So you think she opened it?

00:08:55.543 --> 00:08:58.077
It's a second-Story window, no ledge.

00:08:58.111 --> 00:08:59.677
No one else could have.

00:09:04.244 --> 00:09:06.810
You know this might not
be anything supernatural.

00:09:06.844 --> 00:09:08.443
It might just be pneumonia.

00:09:08.477 --> 00:09:10.710
Maybe. Or maybe something
opened that window.

00:09:10.744 --> 00:09:13.610
I don't know, man. Look, dad
sent us down here for a reason.

00:09:13.644 --> 00:09:15.944
I think we might be
barking up the right tree.

00:09:15.977 --> 00:09:17.044
I'll tell you one thing.

00:09:17.077 --> 00:09:18.044
What?

00:09:18.077 --> 00:09:19.810
That guy we just talked to -

00:09:19.844 --> 00:09:22.610
I'm betting it'll be a
while before he goes home.

00:09:32.244 --> 00:09:34.677
You got anything over there?

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.378
No, nothing.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:39.744
Yeah, me neither.

00:09:50.378 --> 00:09:51.844
Hey, dean.

00:09:51.877 --> 00:09:53.610
Dean: yeah?

00:09:55.111 --> 00:09:59.877
You were right. It's not pneumonia.

00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:05.810
It's rotted.

00:10:09.744 --> 00:10:12.344
What the hell leaves
a handprint like that?

00:10:15.677 --> 00:10:17.410
<i>Man: cheetara.</i>

00:10:17.443 --> 00:10:18.610
<i>Woman: i am sorry to wake you,</i>

00:10:18.644 --> 00:10:20.044
<i>But jaga bids me to bring you to him.</i>

00:10:20.077 --> 00:10:22.077
John: all right.

00:10:23.111 --> 00:10:24.677
You know the drill, dean.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:27.011
If anyone calls, you don't pick up.

00:10:27.044 --> 00:10:30.378
If it's me, i'll ring
once and then call back.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.744
You got that?

00:10:31.777 --> 00:10:35.077
Mm-Hmm. Don't answer the phone
unless it rings once first.

00:10:35.111 --> 00:10:37.710
Come on, dude. Look alive.
This stuff's important.

00:10:37.744 --> 00:10:38.844
I know, it's just,

00:10:38.877 --> 00:10:41.311
We've done it like a million times,

00:10:41.344 --> 00:10:43.144
And you know i'm not stupid.

00:10:43.177 --> 00:10:45.311
I know you're not, but
it only takes one mistake.

00:10:45.344 --> 00:10:46.710
You got that?

00:10:46.744 --> 00:10:50.111
<i>It's important that he join
jaga on the flight deck.</i>

00:10:50.144 --> 00:10:52.710
All right, if i'm not
back sunday night...

00:10:52.744 --> 00:10:54.111
Call pastor jim.

00:10:56.443 --> 00:10:59.011
Lock the doors and
windows, close the shades,

00:10:59.044 --> 00:11:00.244
And most important -

00:11:00.278 --> 00:11:01.810
Watch out for sammy.

00:11:01.844 --> 00:11:04.177
<i>Responsible for lion-O's
welfare, snarf is.</i>

00:11:04.211 --> 00:11:05.443
I know.

00:11:05.477 --> 00:11:07.111
All right, if something
tries to bust in...

00:11:07.144 --> 00:11:10.111
Shoot first, ask questions later.

00:11:10.144 --> 00:11:12.244
That's my man.

00:11:16.211 --> 00:11:17.510
<i>What's up, jaga?</i>

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:18.610
<i>Come closer.</i>

00:11:23.443 --> 00:11:26.111
<i>What's happening to her?</i>

00:11:28.044 --> 00:11:29.911
<i>What was that?</i>

00:11:29.944 --> 00:11:32.510
Dean: i know why dad sent us here.

00:11:37.244 --> 00:11:39.344
He's faced this thing before.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:45.278
He wants us to finish the job.

00:12:07.683 --> 00:12:09.384
So what the hell is a shtriga?

00:12:09.417 --> 00:12:11.317
It's kind of like a witch, i think.

00:12:11.351 --> 00:12:12.984
I don't know much about them.

00:12:13.017 --> 00:12:14.984
Well, i've never heard of it,

00:12:15.017 --> 00:12:17.017
And it's not in dad's journal.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.683
Dad hunted one in fort
douglas, wisconsin,

00:12:19.717 --> 00:12:21.151
About 16, 17 years ago.

00:12:21.184 --> 00:12:24.017
You were there. You don't remember? No.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.518
I guess he caught wind that
the thing's in fitchburg now

00:12:26.551 --> 00:12:28.017
And kicked us the coordinates.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:30.284
So wait, this... shtriga.

00:12:30.317 --> 00:12:32.251
Right, you think it's the
same one dad hunted before?

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:34.783
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:34.817 --> 00:12:36.817
If dad went after it, why
is it still breathing air?

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.984
Because it got away.

00:12:38.017 --> 00:12:39.117
Got away?

00:12:39.151 --> 00:12:40.518
Yeah, sammy, it happens.

00:12:40.551 --> 00:12:41.717
Not very often.

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:43.017
I don't know what to tell you.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.884
Maybe dad didn't have
his wheaties that morning.

00:12:44.917 --> 00:12:46.717
What else do you remember?

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.950
Nothing. I was a kid, all right?

00:12:58.717 --> 00:13:00.351
King or two queens?

00:13:00.384 --> 00:13:01.950
Two queens.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.618
Yeah, i bet.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.817
What'd you say?

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.783
Nice car.

00:13:10.817 --> 00:13:12.950
Hi. Checking in?

00:13:12.984 --> 00:13:14.184
Yeah.

00:13:14.217 --> 00:13:17.750
Uh, do me a favor. Go get
your brother some dinner.

00:13:17.783 --> 00:13:19.551
I'm helping a guest.

00:13:23.184 --> 00:13:25.351
Two queens.

00:13:27.484 --> 00:13:28.783
Funny kid.

00:13:28.817 --> 00:13:30.650
Oh, yeah, he thinks so.

00:13:30.683 --> 00:13:32.417
Will that be cash or credit?

00:13:32.451 --> 00:13:34.050
Do you take mastercard? Mm-Hmm.

00:13:34.084 --> 00:13:35.084
Perfect.

00:13:35.117 --> 00:13:36.184
There you go.

00:13:36.217 --> 00:13:38.618
Thank you.

00:13:54.484 --> 00:13:57.084
When's dad gonna get back?

00:13:57.117 --> 00:13:58.618
Tomorrow.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:13:59.850
When?

00:13:59.884 --> 00:14:00.884
I don't know.

00:14:00.917 --> 00:14:02.750
He usually comes in late, though.

00:14:02.783 --> 00:14:04.518
Now, eat your dinner.

00:14:04.551 --> 00:14:06.783
I'm sick of "scabetti-Os."

00:14:06.817 --> 00:14:09.417
Well, you're the one who wanted them.

00:14:09.451 --> 00:14:10.850
I want lucky charms.

00:14:10.884 --> 00:14:12.451
There's no more lucky charms.

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:13.750
I saw the box.

00:14:13.783 --> 00:14:15.050
Okay, maybe there is,

00:14:15.084 --> 00:14:17.650
But there's only enough
left for one bowl,

00:14:17.683 --> 00:14:19.251
And i haven't had any yet.

00:14:43.017 --> 00:14:45.451
Do you want the prize?

00:14:45.484 --> 00:14:47.884
Sir?

00:14:49.683 --> 00:14:51.717
Thanks.

00:15:02.351 --> 00:15:04.017
Well, you were right.

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:07.783
It wasn't very easy to
find, but you were right.

00:15:07.817 --> 00:15:10.284
A shtriga is a kind of witch.

00:15:10.317 --> 00:15:11.551
They're albanian,

00:15:11.584 --> 00:15:14.518
But legends about them
date back to ancient rome.

00:15:14.551 --> 00:15:16.618
They feed off of spiritus vitae.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.284
Spirit what?

00:15:18.317 --> 00:15:19.584
Vitae. It's latin.

00:15:19.618 --> 00:15:21.683
It translates to "breath of life,"

00:15:21.717 --> 00:15:25.017
Kind of like your life force or essence.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:27.017
Didn't the doctor say the
kids' bodies were wearing out?

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.984
It's a thought.

00:15:29.017 --> 00:15:30.451
You know, she takes your vitality,

00:15:30.484 --> 00:15:32.618
Maybe your immunity goes to
hell, pneumonia takes hold.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:35.850
Anyway, shtrigas can feed
off anyone, but they prefer -

00:15:35.884 --> 00:15:37.618
Children.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:38.884
Yeah.

00:15:38.917 --> 00:15:40.984
Probably because they
have stronger life force.

00:15:41.017 --> 00:15:44.618
And get this
- Shtrigas are invulnerable

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:47.217
To all weapons devised by god and man.

00:15:47.251 --> 00:15:49.451
No, that's not right.

00:15:49.484 --> 00:15:52.950
She's vulnerable when she feeds.

00:15:52.984 --> 00:15:53.984
What?

00:15:54.017 --> 00:15:55.950
If you catch her when she's eating,

00:15:55.984 --> 00:15:58.518
You can blast her with
consecrated wrought irons,

00:15:58.551 --> 00:16:00.384
Buckshots or rounds i think.

00:16:00.417 --> 00:16:02.050
How do you know that?

00:16:02.084 --> 00:16:04.884
Dad told me. I remember.

00:16:04.917 --> 00:16:07.317
Oh.

00:16:07.351 --> 00:16:11.384
So, uh, anything else
dad might have mentioned?

00:16:11.417 --> 00:16:13.717
No, that's it.

00:16:15.783 --> 00:16:17.884
What?

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.917
Nothing.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:25.750
Okay, so, assuming we
can kill it when it eats,

00:16:25.783 --> 00:16:27.584
We've still got to find the thing first,

00:16:27.618 --> 00:16:29.117
Which ain't gonna be a cakewalk.

00:16:29.151 --> 00:16:31.551
Shtrigas take on a human
disguise when they're not hunting.

00:16:31.584 --> 00:16:33.251
What kind of human disguise?

00:16:33.284 --> 00:16:35.084
Historically, something innocuous.

00:16:35.117 --> 00:16:37.917
It could be anything, but it's
usually a feeble old woman,

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:40.950
Which may be how the witches-As-
Old-Crones legend got started.

00:16:40.984 --> 00:16:42.050
Hang on.

00:16:42.084 --> 00:16:43.151
What?

00:16:45.151 --> 00:16:46.384
Check this out.

00:16:46.417 --> 00:16:48.584
I marked down all the
addresses of the victims.

00:16:48.618 --> 00:16:50.618
Now, these are the houses
that have been hit so far,

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:51.850
And dead center -

00:16:51.884 --> 00:16:54.084
The hospital.

00:16:54.117 --> 00:16:57.251
When we were there, i saw
a patient, an old woman.

00:16:57.284 --> 00:16:58.683
An old person, huh?

00:16:58.717 --> 00:16:59.750
Yeah.

00:16:59.783 --> 00:17:00.850
In the hospital?

00:17:00.884 --> 00:17:02.917
Whew! Better call the coast guard.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:04.251
Well, listen, smartass,

00:17:04.284 --> 00:17:06.917
She had an inverted
cross hanging on her wall.

00:17:21.984 --> 00:17:24.151
Betty: good night, dr. Hydaker.

00:17:24.184 --> 00:17:25.717
See you tomorrow, betty.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.850
Try to get some sleep, aaron.

00:17:33.884 --> 00:17:35.284
Come on.

00:18:36.683 --> 00:18:38.884
Who the hell are you?

00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:40.184
Who's there?

00:18:42.317 --> 00:18:44.451
You trying to steal my stuff?

00:18:44.484 --> 00:18:46.351
They're always stealing around here.

00:18:46.384 --> 00:18:49.184
No, ma'am, we're
maintenance. We're sorry.

00:18:49.217 --> 00:18:50.817
We thought you were sleeping.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.551
Ah, nonsense.

00:18:52.584 --> 00:18:54.884
I was sleeping with my peepers open.

00:18:58.351 --> 00:19:01.317
And fix that crucifix, would you?

00:19:01.351 --> 00:19:04.817
I've asked four damn times already.

00:20:02.207 --> 00:20:05.507
"I was sleeping with my peepers open."

00:20:05.541 --> 00:20:08.841
I almost smoked that old gal, i swear.

00:20:08.874 --> 00:20:10.274
It's not funny.

00:20:11.301 --> 00:20:13.534
Oh, man, you should have
seen your face, dean.

00:20:13.567 --> 00:20:16.167
Oh, yeah, laugh it on, man.
We're back to square one.

00:20:18.734 --> 00:20:21.433
Hang on.

00:20:30.067 --> 00:20:32.700
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:32.734 --> 00:20:35.634
My brother's sick.

00:20:35.667 --> 00:20:36.801
The little guy?

00:20:36.834 --> 00:20:38.700
Pneumonia.

00:20:38.734 --> 00:20:41.168
He's in the hospital.

00:20:42.567 --> 00:20:44.300
It's my fault.

00:20:44.333 --> 00:20:46.001
No, come on. How?

00:20:47.168 --> 00:20:49.767
I should have made sure
the window was latched.

00:20:49.801 --> 00:20:52.001
He wouldn't have gotten pneumonia

00:20:52.034 --> 00:20:53.667
If the window was latched.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.667
Listen to me.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:04.134
I can promise you that this
is not your fault, okay?

00:21:04.168 --> 00:21:06.600
It's my job to look after him.

00:21:13.433 --> 00:21:14.834
Michael.

00:21:17.268 --> 00:21:19.834
Turn on the "no vacancy"
sign while i'm gone.

00:21:19.867 --> 00:21:21.600
I've got denise covering room service,

00:21:21.634 --> 00:21:22.700
So don't bother with the rooms.

00:21:22.734 --> 00:21:24.067
I'm going with you. Not now, michael.

00:21:24.101 --> 00:21:25.201
But i got to see asher.

00:21:25.234 --> 00:21:26.667
Dean: hey, michael.

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.034
Hey.

00:21:28.067 --> 00:21:30.834
I know how you feel.
I'm a big brother, too.

00:21:30.867 --> 00:21:33.567
But you got to go easy on
your mom right now, okay?

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:34.767
Aw, damn it.

00:21:34.801 --> 00:21:36.067
I got it.

00:21:36.101 --> 00:21:38.834
Thanks. You're in no condition to drive.

00:21:38.867 --> 00:21:41.600
Why don't you let me give
you a lift to the hospital?

00:21:41.634 --> 00:21:42.934
No, no, i couldn't possibly -

00:21:42.967 --> 00:21:46.567
No, no trouble. I insist.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.500
Be good.

00:22:01.168 --> 00:22:02.901
We're gonna kill this thing.

00:22:02.934 --> 00:22:05.001
I want it dead. You hear me?

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:24.634
Dean: hey.

00:22:24.667 --> 00:22:26.067
Hey, how's the kid?

00:22:26.101 --> 00:22:28.534
He's not good. Where you at?

00:22:28.567 --> 00:22:30.101
I'm at the library,

00:22:30.134 --> 00:22:32.667
Trying to find out as much
as i can about this shtriga.

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:34.333
Yeah, what do you got?

00:22:34.367 --> 00:22:35.567
Well, bad news.

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.801
I started with fort douglas

00:22:37.834 --> 00:22:40.001
Around the time you said dad was there.

00:22:40.034 --> 00:22:41.268
And?

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:42.433
Same deal.

00:22:42.467 --> 00:22:45.834
Before that, there was ogdenville.

00:22:45.867 --> 00:22:49.734
Before that, north
haverbrook and brockway.

00:22:49.767 --> 00:22:53.467
Every 15 to 20 years,
it hits a new town.

00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:56.934
Dean, this thing is just
getting started in fitchburg.

00:22:56.967 --> 00:22:59.867
In all these other places,
it goes on for months,

00:22:59.901 --> 00:23:03.001
Dozens of kids, before the
shtriga finally moves on.

00:23:03.034 --> 00:23:06.600
Kids just languish in
comas, and then they die.

00:23:06.634 --> 00:23:08.801
How far back does this thing go?

00:23:08.834 --> 00:23:09.967
I don't know.

00:23:10.001 --> 00:23:12.667
The earliest mention i
could find is this place

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:15.168
Called black river
falls back in the 1890s.

00:23:15.201 --> 00:23:18.001
Talk about a horror show.

00:23:19.734 --> 00:23:22.001
Whoa.

00:23:22.034 --> 00:23:23.034
Sam?

00:23:23.067 --> 00:23:24.500
Hold on.

00:23:24.534 --> 00:23:26.867
I'm looking at a photograph right now

00:23:26.901 --> 00:23:30.101
Of a bunch of doctors
standing around a kid's bed.

00:23:30.134 --> 00:23:33.001
One of the doctors is hydaker.

00:23:33.034 --> 00:23:34.567
And?

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:37.834
And this picture was taken in 1893.

00:23:37.867 --> 00:23:40.034
You sure?

00:23:40.067 --> 00:23:41.634
Yeah.

00:23:41.667 --> 00:23:44.134
Yeah, absolutely.

00:24:02.634 --> 00:24:06.834
Don't worry. Your son's in good hands.

00:24:06.867 --> 00:24:10.101
I'm gonna take care of him.

00:24:10.134 --> 00:24:13.067
So what's the cdc come up with so far?

00:24:13.101 --> 00:24:15.600
We're still working on a few theories.

00:24:15.634 --> 00:24:18.201
You'll know something as soon as we do.

00:24:18.234 --> 00:24:21.667
Well, nothing's more important
to me than these kids.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:22.667
Hmm.

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:25.034
Just let me know if i can help.

00:24:25.067 --> 00:24:28.268
I'll do that.

00:24:30.600 --> 00:24:33.034
Sam: we should have
thought of this before.

00:24:33.067 --> 00:24:35.500
Doctor's a perfect
disguise. You're trusted.

00:24:35.534 --> 00:24:37.400
You can control the whole thing.

00:24:37.433 --> 00:24:41.433
Huh. That son of a bitch.

00:24:41.467 --> 00:24:43.500
I'm surprised you didn't
draw on him right there.

00:24:43.534 --> 00:24:46.500
Yeah, well...

00:24:46.534 --> 00:24:48.500
First of all,

00:24:48.534 --> 00:24:50.467
I'm not gonna open fire in
a freakin' pediatrics ward.

00:24:50.500 --> 00:24:52.168
Good call.

00:24:52.201 --> 00:24:53.767
Second, it wouldn't have done any good

00:24:53.801 --> 00:24:55.168
Because the bastard's bulletproof

00:24:55.201 --> 00:24:56.767
Unless he's chowing down on something.

00:24:56.801 --> 00:24:58.001
And third, i wasn't packing,

00:24:58.034 --> 00:24:59.567
Which is probably a really good thing

00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:01.700
'Cause i probably would have
just burned a clip in him

00:25:01.734 --> 00:25:03.134
Off of principle alone.

00:25:03.168 --> 00:25:05.734
You're getting wise
in your old age, dean.

00:25:05.767 --> 00:25:06.967
You're damn right.

00:25:07.001 --> 00:25:09.600
'Cause now i know how
we're gonna get it.

00:25:09.634 --> 00:25:11.634
What do you mean?

00:25:11.667 --> 00:25:13.500
The shtriga
- It works through siblings, right?

00:25:13.534 --> 00:25:14.634
Right.

00:25:14.667 --> 00:25:16.034
Well, last night...

00:25:16.067 --> 00:25:17.268
It went after asher.

00:25:17.300 --> 00:25:19.201
Tonight it's probably
gonna come after michael.

00:25:19.234 --> 00:25:20.367
Then we got to get him out of here.

00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:22.667
No. No, that would blow the whole deal.

00:25:22.700 --> 00:25:24.168
What? Yeah.

00:25:24.201 --> 00:25:26.600
Then you want to use the kid as bait?

00:25:27.667 --> 00:25:30.433
Are you nuts? No. Forget it.
That's out of the question.

00:25:30.467 --> 00:25:32.967
Sam, it's the only way
- If this thing disappears,

00:25:33.001 --> 00:25:35.300
It could be years before
we get another chance.

00:25:35.333 --> 00:25:37.067
Michael's a kid, and
i'm not gonna dangle him

00:25:37.101 --> 00:25:38.834
In front of that thing
like a worm on a hook.

00:25:38.867 --> 00:25:40.834
Dad did not send me here to walk away.

00:25:40.867 --> 00:25:43.034
<i>Send you here? He didn't send you here.</i>

00:25:43.067 --> 00:25:45.268
<i>He sent us here. This
isn't about you, sam.</i>

00:25:45.300 --> 00:25:47.101
I'm the one that screwed
up. It's my fault.

00:25:47.134 --> 00:25:49.201
There's no telling how
many kids have gotten hurt

00:25:49.234 --> 00:25:50.333
Because of me.

00:25:50.367 --> 00:25:53.934
What are you saying,
dean? How is it your fault?

00:25:59.734 --> 00:26:01.168
Dean.

00:26:01.201 --> 00:26:04.433
You've been hiding
something from the get-Go.

00:26:04.467 --> 00:26:07.101
Since when does dad bail on a hunt?

00:26:07.134 --> 00:26:10.168
Since when does he
let something get away?

00:26:10.201 --> 00:26:15.400
Now, talk to me, man.
Tell me what's going on.

00:26:24.967 --> 00:26:27.734
Fort douglas, wisconsin.

00:26:27.767 --> 00:26:30.767
It was the third night
in this crap room,

00:26:30.801 --> 00:26:33.400
And i was climbing the walls, man.

00:26:33.433 --> 00:26:35.234
I needed to get some air.

00:26:35.268 --> 00:26:36.867
<i>...if ever i saw one.</i>

00:26:36.901 --> 00:26:38.500
<i>Command performance.</i>

00:27:05.433 --> 00:27:06.767
Hey, kid.

00:27:07.934 --> 00:27:09.934
We're closing up.

00:28:13.333 --> 00:28:14.634
Get out of the way!

00:28:24.967 --> 00:28:29.201
Sammy. Sammy. Sammy.

00:28:29.234 --> 00:28:30.500
You okay?

00:28:30.534 --> 00:28:33.268
Sam: dad, what's going on?

00:28:33.300 --> 00:28:35.134
Are you all right?

00:28:38.734 --> 00:28:42.134
What happened?

00:28:42.168 --> 00:28:44.201
I
- I just went out.

00:28:44.234 --> 00:28:45.901
What?

00:28:45.934 --> 00:28:48.567
J
- Just for a second. I'm sorry.

00:28:48.600 --> 00:28:50.967
I told you not to leave this room.

00:28:51.001 --> 00:28:53.967
I told you not to let
him out of your sight.

00:29:06.168 --> 00:29:10.433
Dad just grabbed us and booked,

00:29:10.467 --> 00:29:16.001
Dropped us off at pastor
jim's about three hours away.

00:29:16.034 --> 00:29:18.801
By the time he got back to fort douglas,

00:29:18.834 --> 00:29:20.700
The shtriga had disappeared.

00:29:20.734 --> 00:29:22.967
It was just gone.

00:29:26.001 --> 00:29:30.168
It never resurfaced until now.

00:29:30.201 --> 00:29:33.168
Dad never spoke about it again.

00:29:33.201 --> 00:29:36.201
I didn't ask.

00:29:36.234 --> 00:29:38.734
But he, uh...

00:29:40.901 --> 00:29:46.001
He looked at me different,
you know, which was worse.

00:29:46.034 --> 00:29:47.500
Not that i blame him.

00:29:47.534 --> 00:29:50.400
He gave me an order,
and i didn't listen,

00:29:50.433 --> 00:29:52.567
And i almost got you killed.

00:29:52.600 --> 00:29:54.001
You were just a kid.

00:29:54.034 --> 00:29:58.001
Don't.

00:29:58.034 --> 00:30:02.534
Dad knew this was
unfinished business for me.

00:30:02.567 --> 00:30:05.767
He sent me here to finish it.

00:30:07.834 --> 00:30:11.634
But using michael
- I don't know, dean.

00:30:11.667 --> 00:30:14.867
I mean, how about one of
us hides under the cover?

00:30:14.901 --> 00:30:17.767
You know, we'll be the bait.

00:30:17.801 --> 00:30:20.767
No, that won't work.

00:30:20.801 --> 00:30:23.801
It's got to get close
enough to feed. It'll see us.

00:30:26.367 --> 00:30:28.867
Believe me, i don't like it,
but it's got to be the kid.

00:30:34.467 --> 00:30:36.433
Michael: you're crazy!

00:30:36.467 --> 00:30:39.067
Just go away or i'm calling the cops.

00:30:39.101 --> 00:30:41.134
Hang on a second. Just listen to me.

00:30:41.168 --> 00:30:43.634
You have to believe me, okay?

00:30:43.667 --> 00:30:45.234
This thing came through the window

00:30:45.268 --> 00:30:46.433
And attacked your brother.

00:30:49.001 --> 00:30:50.067
I've seen it.

00:30:50.101 --> 00:30:51.600
I know what it looks like

00:30:51.634 --> 00:30:54.101
'Cause it attacked my brother once, too.

00:31:01.333 --> 00:31:03.268
This thing -

00:31:03.300 --> 00:31:05.934
Is it, like...

00:31:05.967 --> 00:31:10.500
It has this long, black robe?

00:31:10.534 --> 00:31:12.767
You saw it last night, didn't you?

00:31:12.801 --> 00:31:16.767
I thought i was having a nightmare.

00:31:18.834 --> 00:31:22.801
I'd give anything not to tell you this,

00:31:22.834 --> 00:31:24.901
But sometimes nightmares are real.

00:31:24.934 --> 00:31:28.034
<i>So why are you telling me?</i>

00:31:28.067 --> 00:31:29.834
Because we need your help.

00:31:29.867 --> 00:31:31.234
My help?

00:31:31.268 --> 00:31:36.001
We can kill it, me and
him. It's what we do.

00:31:36.034 --> 00:31:38.067
But we can't do it without you.

00:31:38.101 --> 00:31:41.300
What? No.

00:31:41.333 --> 00:31:43.034
Michael, listen to me.

00:31:43.067 --> 00:31:44.801
This thing hurt asher,

00:31:44.834 --> 00:31:48.034
And it's gonna keep hurting
kids unless we stop it.

00:31:48.067 --> 00:31:49.500
Do you understand me?

00:31:52.201 --> 00:31:55.134
Well, that went crappy. Now what?

00:31:55.168 --> 00:31:56.333
What did you expect?

00:31:56.367 --> 00:31:58.934
You can't ask an adult
to do something like that,

00:31:58.967 --> 00:32:00.667
Much less a kid.

00:32:08.901 --> 00:32:11.734
If you kill it, will asher get better?

00:32:16.534 --> 00:32:20.067
Honestly, we don't know.

00:32:23.101 --> 00:32:26.001
You said you're a big brother.

00:32:26.034 --> 00:32:28.234
Yeah.

00:32:28.268 --> 00:32:30.101
You'd take care of your little brother?

00:32:30.134 --> 00:32:33.967
You'd do anything for him?

00:32:34.001 --> 00:32:36.234
Yeah, i would.

00:32:38.134 --> 00:32:41.934
Me too.

00:32:41.967 --> 00:32:43.333
I'll help.

00:33:04.470 --> 00:33:06.104
This camera has night vision on it,

00:33:06.138 --> 00:33:08.138
So we'll be able to
see you as clear as day.

00:33:08.170 --> 00:33:09.370
Are we good?

00:33:09.404 --> 00:33:10.537
Hair to the right.

00:33:10.570 --> 00:33:12.470
There, there.

00:33:12.504 --> 00:33:15.771
Michael: what do i do?

00:33:15.804 --> 00:33:19.404
Just stay under the covers.

00:33:19.437 --> 00:33:22.937
And if it shows up?

00:33:22.971 --> 00:33:24.837
Well, we'll be right in the next room.

00:33:24.871 --> 00:33:27.437
We're gonna come in with
guns, so as soon as we do,

00:33:27.470 --> 00:33:29.804
You roll off this bed
and you crawl under it.

00:33:31.871 --> 00:33:33.604
What if you shoot me?

00:33:33.637 --> 00:33:36.203
We won't shoot you. We're good shots.

00:33:37.837 --> 00:33:41.071
We're not gonna fire
until you're clear, okay?

00:33:41.104 --> 00:33:43.570
Have you heard a gunshot before?

00:33:43.604 --> 00:33:45.237
Like in the movies?

00:33:45.270 --> 00:33:48.837
It's gonna be a lot
louder than in the movies.

00:33:48.871 --> 00:33:52.470
So i want you to stay under
the bed, cover your ears,

00:33:52.504 --> 00:33:55.737
And do not come out until
we say so, you understand?

00:33:58.504 --> 00:34:01.337
Michael, are you sure
you want to do this?

00:34:01.370 --> 00:34:03.104
You don't have to. It's
okay. I won't be mad.

00:34:03.138 --> 00:34:05.138
No, i'm okay.

00:34:05.170 --> 00:34:07.971
Just don't shoot me.

00:34:08.004 --> 00:34:11.237
We're not gonna let
anything happen to you.

00:34:11.270 --> 00:34:12.570
I promise.

00:34:25.370 --> 00:34:26.737
What time is it?

00:34:28.837 --> 00:34:30.004
3:00.

00:34:32.038 --> 00:34:33.871
You sure these iron
rounds are gonna work?

00:34:35.837 --> 00:34:37.270
Consecrated iron rounds.

00:34:37.303 --> 00:34:40.937
And yeah, it's what dad used last time.

00:34:40.971 --> 00:34:43.671
Hey, dean, i'm sorry.

00:34:46.504 --> 00:34:47.570
For what?

00:34:50.203 --> 00:34:52.104
You know...

00:34:52.138 --> 00:34:55.237
I've really given you a lot of crap

00:34:55.270 --> 00:34:58.804
For always following dad's orders,

00:34:58.837 --> 00:35:02.303
But i know why you do it.

00:35:02.337 --> 00:35:04.337
Oh, god. Kill me now.

00:35:09.604 --> 00:35:10.671
Wait, look.

00:35:45.470 --> 00:35:47.104
Now? Not yet.

00:36:21.570 --> 00:36:23.104
Michael, down!

00:36:33.270 --> 00:36:34.971
Mike, you all right? Yeah.

00:36:35.004 --> 00:36:37.704
Just sit tight.

00:37:00.170 --> 00:37:01.203
Dean!

00:37:31.637 --> 00:37:33.537
Dean: hey!

00:37:36.637 --> 00:37:38.437
You okay, little brother?

00:38:11.004 --> 00:38:12.937
It's okay, michael. You can come on out.

00:38:45.477 --> 00:38:47.544
Hey, joanna, how's asher doing?

00:38:47.577 --> 00:38:49.611
Have you seen michael?
Michael: mom! Mom!

00:38:49.644 --> 00:38:51.244
Hey!

00:38:52.744 --> 00:38:53.943
How's ash?

00:38:53.977 --> 00:38:56.077
I've got some good news.
Your brother's gonna be fine.

00:38:56.110 --> 00:38:57.277
Really?

00:38:57.310 --> 00:38:59.277
Yeah, really. No one can explain it.

00:38:59.310 --> 00:39:02.144
It's, uh, it's a miracle.

00:39:02.177 --> 00:39:04.310
They're gonna keep him in
overnight for observation,

00:39:04.344 --> 00:39:05.811
But after that, he's coming home.

00:39:05.844 --> 00:39:06.878
That's great.

00:39:06.910 --> 00:39:09.411
How are all the other kids doing?

00:39:09.444 --> 00:39:10.644
Good, real good.

00:39:10.677 --> 00:39:12.744
A bunch of them should be
checking out in a few days.

00:39:12.778 --> 00:39:15.277
Dr. Travis says the ward's
gonna be like a ghost town.

00:39:15.310 --> 00:39:18.544
Dr. Travis? What about dr. Hydaker?

00:39:18.577 --> 00:39:19.644
Oh, he wasn't in today.

00:39:19.677 --> 00:39:21.377
He must have been sick or something.

00:39:21.411 --> 00:39:23.943
Yeah, yeah, must have.

00:39:23.977 --> 00:39:28.110
So did anything happen while i was gone?

00:39:28.144 --> 00:39:30.110
No, same old stuff.

00:39:30.144 --> 00:39:31.910
Okay. You can go see ash.

00:39:31.943 --> 00:39:33.444
Now? Only if you want to.

00:39:38.043 --> 00:39:39.310
I better get going

00:39:39.344 --> 00:39:41.577
Before he hot-Wires the
car and drives himself.

00:39:48.110 --> 00:39:51.811
It's too bad.

